<LocalTag Name="Wrk_CylRetract" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" ExternalAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Internal copy of Out_CylRetract]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_CylExtend" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" ExternalAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Internal copy of Out_CylExtend]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_Unlock" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" ExternalAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Internal copy of Out_Unlock]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_Lock" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" ExternalAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Internal copy of Out_Lock]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_Dec" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" ExternalAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Internal copy of Out_Dec]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_Inc" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" ExternalAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Internal copy of Out_Inc]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_MaintTrig" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" ExternalAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Device is Moving or in Maintenance and retriggerable]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_LockFail" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" ExternalAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Lock Fail Fault (latched) de-energizes device and requires reset]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_PosFail" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" ExternalAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Position Fail Fault (latched) de-energizes device and requires reset]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Inf_Type" DataType="STRING_16" ExternalAccess="Read Only">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Type identifier for HMI navigation]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>06 00 00 00 50 5F 6E 50 6F 73 00 00 00 00 00 00 
00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="String" Length="6">
<![CDATA['P_nPos']]>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_LockFailSts" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" ExternalAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Buffer bit for Sts_LockFail]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_PosFailSts" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" ExternalAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Buffer bit for Sts_PosFail]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Inf_Lib" DataType="STRING_12" ExternalAccess="Read Only">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Display Library for Faceplate call-up]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>06 00 00 00 52 41 2D 42 41 53 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="String" Length="6">
<![CDATA['RA-BAS']]>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_SrcQ" DataType="SINT" Radix="Decimal" ExternalAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Register for building Source / Quality enumeration]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="SINT" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_NotRdy" DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" ExternalAccess="None">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Device Not Ready conditions excluding shed latches]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
<DefaultData Format="Decorated">
<DataValue DataType="BOOL" Radix="Decimal" Value="0"/>
</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
</LocalTags>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="EnableInFalse" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Disabled is asserted; Outputs OFF; Device Status shown based on feedbacks if possible, but Alarms disabled]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
OFF-SCAN (EnableIn is False) STATUS
============================================================
If this Valve is OFF-SCAN (rung is false or EnableIn is false in FBD), then:

Handle "NO MODE" Selection using the standard P_Mode AOI (EnableInFalse Routine, false scan required!).

NOTE:  IN ORDER TO AVOID USING AN "AFI" (which will generate a routine verify warning),
THIS RUNG USES AN XIC of Cfg_PCmdClear, followed by an XIO of the SAME BIT
to ensure P_Mode is SCANNED FALSE ("NO MODE").

THIS IS NOT DEAD CODE AND MUST APPEAR EXACTLY AS SHOWN FOR PROPER OPERATION!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear)XIO(Cfg_PCmdClear)P_Mode(Mode);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[First-Come First-Served Ownership Arbitration still needs to happen, even when device is disabled.
If a requestor supplies a non-zero Owner ID and the current owner is NONE (zero),
Ownership is assigned to the requesting ID.  When that requestor sets the Owner ID back
to zero, Ownership is relinquished back to NONE.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[EQU(PSet_Owner,0) ,EQU(Val_Owner,0) ]MOV(PSet_Owner,Val_Owner);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA["Lurking" Program Commands are cleared if they are set as "Edge" triggered
(cleared by this object as received).
(Lurking Acknowledge Commands are left to perform their action.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear)[OTU(PCmd_Pos1) OTU(PCmd_Pos2) OTU(PCmd_Pos3) OTU(PCmd_Pos4) ,OTU(PCmd_Pos5) OTU(PCmd_Pos6) OTU(PCmd_Pos7) OTU(PCmd_Pos8) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA["Lurking" Operator Commands are cleared, as well as Program Reset.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(OCmd_Pos1) OTU(OCmd_Pos2) OTU(OCmd_Pos3) OTU(OCmd_Pos4) ,OTU(OCmd_Pos5) OTU(OCmd_Pos6) OTU(OCmd_Pos7) OTU(OCmd_Pos8) ,OTU(OCmd_Bypass) OTU(OCmd_Check) OTU(MCmd_Disable) OTU(MCmd_Enable) ,OTU(OCmd_Reset) OTU(OCmd_ResetAckAll) OTU(PCmd_Reset) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Override Command is set to NONE.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Since we're not processing Operator Commands, we're not READY for them either!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(Rdy_Pos1) OTU(Rdy_Pos2) OTU(Rdy_Pos3) OTU(Rdy_Pos4) ,OTU(Rdy_Pos5) OTU(Rdy_Pos6) OTU(Rdy_Pos7) OTU(Rdy_Pos8) ,OTU(Rdy_Bypass) OTU(Rdy_Check) OTU(Rdy_Disable) OTU(Rdy_Enable) ,OTU(Rdy_Reset) OTU(Rdy_ResetAckAll) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
FEEDBACK INPUT GATHERING
============================================================
If the device has position feedback and is not being simulated,
the Position Feedback bits are collected into a single word.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_UsePosFdbk)XIO(Inp_Sim)[CLR(Wrk_Inp) ,XIC(Inp_Pos1Fdbk) OTE(Wrk_Inp.1) ,XIC(Inp_Pos2Fdbk) OTE(Wrk_Inp.2) ,XIC(Inp_Pos3Fdbk) OTE(Wrk_Inp.3) ,XIC(Inp_Pos4Fdbk) OTE(Wrk_Inp.4) ,XIC(Inp_Pos5Fdbk) OTE(Wrk_Inp.5) ,XIC(Inp_Pos6Fdbk) OTE(Wrk_Inp.6) ,XIC(Inp_Pos7Fdbk) OTE(Wrk_Inp.7) ,XIC(Inp_Pos8Fdbk) OTE(Wrk_Inp.8) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the word containing the position feedbacks contains SPECIFIC VALUES of
2, 4, 8, ..., 256, then a single feedback bit is being received for a specific position.
Any other value indicates that the device has no feedbacks set (value is zero)
or multiple feedbacks set (value is non-zero and not one of the above value.

If a single feedback is set, report that as the device position.
Otherwise, return Actual Position of zero (moving).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[MOV(9,Wrk_Fdbk) ,XIC(Cfg_UsePosFdbk) XIO(Inp_Sim) [EQU(Wrk_Inp,0) CLR(Wrk_Fdbk) OTE(Sts_Moving) ,EQU(Wrk_Inp,2) MOV(1,Wrk_Fdbk) OTE(Sts_Pos1) ,EQU(Wrk_Inp,4) GEQ(Cfg_NumPos,2) MOV(2,Wrk_Fdbk) OTE(Sts_Pos2) ,EQU(Wrk_Inp,8) GEQ(Cfg_NumPos,3) MOV(3,Wrk_Fdbk) OTE(Sts_Pos3) ,EQU(Wrk_Inp,16) GEQ(Cfg_NumPos,4) MOV(4,Wrk_Fdbk) OTE(Sts_Pos4) ,EQU(Wrk_Inp,32) GEQ(Cfg_NumPos,5) MOV(5,Wrk_Fdbk) OTE(Sts_Pos5) ,EQU(Wrk_Inp,64) GEQ(Cfg_NumPos,6) MOV(6,Wrk_Fdbk) OTE(Sts_Pos6) ,EQU(Wrk_Inp,128) GEQ(Cfg_NumPos,7) MOV(7,Wrk_Fdbk) OTE(Sts_Pos7) ,EQU(Wrk_Inp,256) EQU(Cfg_NumPos,8) MOV(8,Wrk_Fdbk) OTE(Sts_Pos8) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Clear the latched Shed faults and alarms, and reset the instruction's timers and retry counter.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx).  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(Nrdy_IOFault) OTU(Wrk_PosFail) OTU(Wrk_PosFailSts) OTU(Wrk_LockFail) OTU(Wrk_LockFailSts) ,RES(Wrk_PosChkT) RES(Wrk_Pos1ChkT) RES(Wrk_LockChkT) RES(Wrk_UnlockChkT) ,RES(Wrk_VerifyT) RES(Wrk_ExtendT) CLR(Wrk_RetryC) ,RES(Wrk_PosSimT) RES(Wrk_LockSimT) RES(Wrk_RightLeftSimT) RES(Wrk_ExtRetrSimT) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Outputs are cleared when Disabled.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_Out) OTU(Out_Pos1) OTU(Out_Pos2) OTU(Out_Pos3) OTU(Out_Pos4) ,OTU(Out_Pos5) OTU(Out_Pos6) OTU(Out_Pos7) OTU(Out_Pos8) ,OTU(Out_Inc) OTU(Out_Dec) OTU(Out_Unlock) OTU(Out_Lock) ,OTU(Out_CylExtend) OTU(Out_CylRetract) OTU(Out_CylLeft) OTU(Out_CylRight) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Show the device as Disabled and Not Ready, not Available, and with no
Maintenance Bypass breadcrumb.
Show the device feedback status.
Show the enumerated device command as NONE.
Show the enumerated device status as DISABLED.
Show the enumerated device fault status as NONE.
Show the internal device state as POWERUP / UNKNOWN.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTL(Sts_Disabled) OTL(Sts_NotRdy) OTU(Sts_Available) OTU(Sts_MaintByp) ,OTL(Nrdy_NoMode) OTU(Nrdy_Disabled) OTU(Nrdy_CfgErr) OTU(Nrdy_Intlk) ,OTU(Nrdy_Perm) OTU(Nrdy_Fail) OTU(Nrdy_IOFault) ,MOV(Wrk_Fdbk,Val_Fdbk) CLR(Val_Cmd) MOV(33,Val_Sts) CLR(Val_Fault) CLR(Val_State) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ENUMERATED SOURCE / QUALITY VALUES
============================================================
Source and Quality for Input / Output values / status (SrcQ_IO)

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[MOV(20,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Inp_IOFault) MOV(34,Wrk_SrcQ) ,MOV(Wrk_SrcQ,SrcQ_IO) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Source and Quality for primary values / status (SrcQ)

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(20,SrcQ);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Clear the Alarms and the Notify Status, and show the Alarms Inhibited breadcrumb.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(Alm_PosFail) OTU(Alm_LockFail) OTU(Alm_IntlkTrip) OTU(Alm_IOFault) ,OTU(Sts_PosFail) OTU(Sts_LockFail) OTU(Sts_IntlkTrip) OTU(Sts_IOFault) ,OTL(Sts_AlmInh) CLR(Val_Notify) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Normal Scan: control / monitor multi-position device]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Copyright © Rockwell Automation, Inc.  All Rights Reserved.
============================================================
P_nPOS:  PROCESS -- n-POSITION DEVICE
============================================================
Revision 3.1-02 Release  2014-09-30:  See V3.1-xx Release Notes for details.
V2.x Revision History archived.
V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Inf_Lib. Using P_Alarm V3.0, P_Mode V3.0.
V3.0-01  2013-07-31:  Modified Parameter descriptions only.
V3.0-02  2013-09-03:  Modified Parameter descriptions only.
V3.0-03  2013-10-30:  Corrected Parameter descriptions and default
configuration values for alarms only.
V3.0-04  2014-01-22:  Modified to fix position simulation.
V3.1-00  2014-07-08:  Modified to use P_Alarm, P_Mode V3.1.Added Not Ready
 reason bits (Nrdy_Xxxxx), source/quality values (SrcQ).
Modified to consistently use alias tag names
V3.1-01  2014-09-03:  Exposed fail timers ACC/PRE (read-only). Corrections to
Nrdy_ trip and reset logic. Using P_Alarm, P_Mode V3.1-01.
V3.1-02  2014-09-30:  Unchanged, but using P_Alarm V3.1-02.
============================================================
This Instruction controls and monitors a Multi-Position Device (up to eight positions).
Examples of such devices include Rotary Tube Selector Valves (RTSVs),
multi-position slide-gate valves, and other multi-position valves, dampers, etc.

This instruction also supports:
*  Monitoring of limit switch or other position feedback, display of actual Device position
*  Detection of failure to reach the next requested position
*  Monitoring of Permissive conditions to allow moving
*  Monitoring of Interlock conditions to de-energize or force move to
position 1 (configurable)
*  Optiounal handling of a position lock, seal or other function which must be
"unlocked" to allow motion
*  Outputs for each position, for increase/decrease, and for indexing
cylinders or other actuators to "step" the position
*  Simulation, providing feedback of a working Device while disabling outputs
*  Monitoring of I/O communication faults
*  Alarms for Failure to reach position, failure to unlock or lock optional locking
function, Interlock Trip, I/O Fault
*  "Available" status for use by automation logic to know whether Device
      can be controlled by other objects.

Modes are provided by a P_Mode AOI instance.
Alarms are provided by P_Alarm AOI instances.
Modes of operation: Operator, Program, Override, Maintenance, Hand
============================================================
SHOW LOCAL STRINGS
============================================================
The STRINGs containing the text associated with each instance of this
instruction cannot be Input or Output Parameters, because STRINGs are not
 'atomic' types. (Inputs and Outputs must be SINT, INT, DINT, REAL, or BOOL.)

In order to make it easier to find and configure these STRINGs, this rung
was added.  THE JMP (and the LBL on the following rung)
MUST NOT BE REMOVED!!!

To view the STRINGs, go to the instruction instance (in LD or FBD), RIGHT-click
to bring up the context menu and select "Open Instruction Logic".
This rung will appear with the STRING values for the selected instance.
You may double-click the STRING values here to modify them as well.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[JMP(SkipText)[CONCAT(Cfg_Desc,Cfg_Label,Cfg_Tag) LOWER(Cfg_Pos1Name,Cfg_Pos2Name) LOWER(Cfg_Pos3Name,Cfg_Pos4Name) ,LOWER(Cfg_Pos5Name,Cfg_Pos6Name) LOWER(Cfg_Pos7Name,Cfg_Pos8Name) LOWER(Inf_Lib,Inf_Type) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
MODE PROCESSING
============================================================
This rung handles received Mode Inputs and Commands:

NOTE:  All Commands for Mode, Alarm are aliased directly to the
corresponding Commands in the contained P_Mode and P_Alarm AOIs.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(SkipText)P_Mode(Mode);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung handles simple First-Come First-Served Ownership Arbitration.
If a requestor supplies a non-zero Owner ID and the current owner is NONE (zero),
Ownership is assigned to the requesting ID.  When that requestor sets the Owner ID back
to zero, Ownership is relinquished back to NONE.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[EQU(PSet_Owner,0) ,EQU(Val_Owner,0) ]MOV(PSet_Owner,Val_Owner);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
CONFIGURATION PROCESSING
============================================================
If the device is configured to NOT HAVE Position Feedback, then Position Feedback is not USED.

If the device is configured to NOT HAVE a Lock function at all, then it cannot HAVE Lock Feedback.

If the device is configured to NOT HAVE Lock Feedback, then Lock Feedback is not USED.

If the device is configured to NOT HAVE Cylinder Feedback (for the indexing
function), then Cylinder Feedback is not USED.

If the device is NOT configured to be Circular (rotary), it cannot be "clockwise only" --
it must be able to move bi-directionally.

If the device IS configured to be Circular (rotary), it makes no sense to return to
position 1 during every move -- ]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_HasPosFdbk) OTU(Cfg_UsePosFdbk) ,XIO(Cfg_HasLock) OTU(Cfg_HasLockFdbk) ,XIO(Cfg_HasLockFdbk) OTU(Cfg_UseLockFdbk) ,XIO(Cfg_HasCylFdbk) OTU(Cfg_UseCylFdbk) ,XIO(Cfg_Circ) OTU(Cfg_CWOnly) ,XIC(Cfg_Circ) OTU(Cfg_ViaPos1) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[These rungs get Configuration data (such as timer presets) and distribute as needed.
Note that some Configuration data are used directly in-place.

If any timer preset is invalid (outside the range of 0 to 2147483647 ms),
it could cause a negative timer preset, which would fault the controller.
Flag any invalid timer preset and make the timer preset a value which will not fault.

Enter the time (in seconds) to allow the Device to move to its target position.
Enter the time (in seconds) to allow the Device to lock or unlock.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[[MUL(Cfg_PosChkT,1000,Wrk_PosChkT.PRE) XIC(Wrk_PosChkT.PRE.31) MOV(2147483647,Wrk_PosChkT.PRE) ,MUL(Cfg_LockChkT,1000,Wrk_LockChkT.PRE) XIC(Wrk_LockChkT.PRE.31) MOV(2147483647,Wrk_LockChkT.PRE) ] OTE(Err_Fail) ,MOV(Wrk_PosChkT.PRE,Wrk_Pos1ChkT.PRE) ,MOV(Wrk_LockChkT.PRE,Wrk_UnlockChkT.PRE) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Enter the delay time once the device reaches position before verifying it did not coast through.
Enter the delay before extending the cylinder when using the cylinder indexing method of motion.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[MUL(Cfg_VerifyT,1000,Wrk_VerifyT.PRE) XIC(Wrk_VerifyT.PRE.31) CLR(Wrk_VerifyT.PRE) ,MUL(Cfg_ExtendT,1000,Wrk_ExtendT.PRE) XIC(Wrk_ExtendT.PRE.31) CLR(Wrk_ExtendT.PRE) ]OTE(Err_Timer);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If any of the Device Simulation Timer presets is invalid (outside the range of
0 to 2147483647 ms), flag a Simulation Configuration Error (and make the timer
preset valid so we don't fault the controller).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[[MUL(Cfg_PosSimT,1000,Wrk_PosSimT.PRE) XIC(Wrk_PosSimT.PRE.31) CLR(Wrk_PosSimT.PRE) ,MUL(Cfg_LockSimT,1000,Wrk_LockSimT.PRE) XIC(Wrk_LockSimT.PRE.31) CLR(Wrk_LockSimT.PRE) ,MUL(Cfg_CylSimT,1000,Wrk_ExtRetrSimT.PRE) XIC(Wrk_ExtRetrSimT.PRE.31) CLR(Wrk_ExtRetrSimT.PRE) ] OTE(Err_Sim) ,MOV(Wrk_ExtRetrSimT.PRE,Wrk_RightLeftSimT.PRE) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung generates a summary Bad Config status, simply an OR of the Err_ bits provided above
(in the Configuration handling section) with the alarm Err_ bits ORed with
the error for invalid number of device positions (must be 2 to 8).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[LIM(9,Cfg_NumPos,1) OTE(Err_NumPos) ,XIC(Err_Fail) ,XIC(Err_Timer) ,XIC(Err_Sim) ,[XIC(PosFail.Sts_Err) ,XIC(LockFail.Sts_Err) ,XIC(IntlkTrip.Sts_Err) ,XIC(IOFault.Sts_Err) ] OTE(Err_Alarm) ]OTE(Sts_Err);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
FEEDBACK INPUT GATHERING
============================================================
If the device has position feedback and is not being simulated,
the Position Feedback bits are collected into a single word.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_UsePosFdbk)XIO(Inp_Sim)[CLR(Wrk_Inp) ,XIC(Inp_Pos1Fdbk) OTE(Wrk_Inp.1) ,XIC(Inp_Pos2Fdbk) OTE(Wrk_Inp.2) ,XIC(Inp_Pos3Fdbk) OTE(Wrk_Inp.3) ,XIC(Inp_Pos4Fdbk) OTE(Wrk_Inp.4) ,XIC(Inp_Pos5Fdbk) OTE(Wrk_Inp.5) ,XIC(Inp_Pos6Fdbk) OTE(Wrk_Inp.6) ,XIC(Inp_Pos7Fdbk) OTE(Wrk_Inp.7) ,XIC(Inp_Pos8Fdbk) OTE(Wrk_Inp.8) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the word containing the position feedbacks contains SPECIFIC VALUES of
2, 4, 8, ..., 256, then a single feedback bit is being received for a specific position.
Any other value indicates that the device has no feedbacks set (value is zero)
or multiple feedbacks set (value is non-zero and not one of the above value.

If a single feedback is set, report that as the device position.
Otherwise, return Actual Position of zero (moving).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_UsePosFdbk)XIO(Inp_Sim)[MOV(9,Wrk_Fdbk) ,EQU(Wrk_Inp,0) CLR(Wrk_Fdbk) ,EQU(Wrk_Inp,2) MOV(1,Wrk_Fdbk) ,EQU(Wrk_Inp,4) MOV(2,Wrk_Fdbk) ,EQU(Wrk_Inp,8) GEQ(Cfg_NumPos,3) MOV(3,Wrk_Fdbk) ,EQU(Wrk_Inp,16) GEQ(Cfg_NumPos,4) MOV(4,Wrk_Fdbk) ,EQU(Wrk_Inp,32) GEQ(Cfg_NumPos,5) MOV(5,Wrk_Fdbk) ,EQU(Wrk_Inp,64) GEQ(Cfg_NumPos,6) MOV(6,Wrk_Fdbk) ,EQU(Wrk_Inp,128) GEQ(Cfg_NumPos,7) MOV(7,Wrk_Fdbk) ,EQU(Wrk_Inp,256) EQU(Cfg_NumPos,8) MOV(8,Wrk_Fdbk) ,MOV(Wrk_Fdbk,Val_Fdbk) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If Lock Feedback is being used and the device is not in simulation,
set the internal Locked and Unlocked feedback bits based on the inputs.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_UseLockFdbk)XIO(Inp_Sim)[OTU(Wrk_LockFdbk) OTU(Wrk_UnlockFdbk) ,XIC(Inp_LockFdbk) XIO(Inp_UnlockFdbk) OTL(Wrk_LockFdbk) ,XIO(Inp_LockFdbk) XIC(Inp_UnlockFdbk) OTL(Wrk_UnlockFdbk) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If Cylinder Feedback is being used and the device is not in simulation,
set the internal cylinder position feedback bits based on the inputs.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_UseCylFdbk)XIO(Inp_Sim)[OTU(Wrk_CylExtFdbk) OTU(Wrk_CylLeftFdbk) OTU(Wrk_CylRetrFdbk) OTU(Wrk_CylRightFdbk) ,XIC(Inp_CylExtFdbk) XIO(Inp_CylRetrFdbk) OTL(Wrk_CylExtFdbk) ,XIC(Inp_CylLeftFdbk) XIO(Inp_CylRightFdbk) OTL(Wrk_CylLeftFdbk) ,XIO(Inp_CylExtFdbk) XIC(Inp_CylRetrFdbk) OTL(Wrk_CylRetrFdbk) ,XIO(Inp_CylLeftFdbk) XIC(Inp_CylRightFdbk) OTL(Wrk_CylRightFdbk) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If Position feedback is NOT used, because of Simulation or Configuration,
use sim timers to simulate motion through intermediate positions.\

#####  V3.0-04  2014-01-20:  Modified to fix position simulation  #####

@@@@@  A timer is doubled to ensure it sets or clears the  @@@@@
@@@@@  .DN bit the same scan if the timer preset is zero.  @@@@@]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_UsePosFdbk) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) ][[XIC(Wrk_Inc) ,XIC(Wrk_Dec) ] XIO(Wrk_PosSimT.DN) TON(Wrk_PosSimT,?,?) TON(Wrk_PosSimT,?,?) ,XIC(Wrk_PosSimT.DN) [XIC(Wrk_Inc) ADD(Wrk_Fdbk,1,Wrk_Fdbk) ,XIC(Wrk_Dec) SUB(Wrk_Fdbk,1,Wrk_Fdbk) ] ,GRT(Wrk_Fdbk,Cfg_NumPos) MOV(1,Wrk_Fdbk) ,LEQ(Wrk_Fdbk,0) MOV(Cfg_NumPos,Wrk_Fdbk) ,MOV(Wrk_Fdbk,Val_Fdbk) XIC(Wrk_PosSimT.TT) CMP(Wrk_PosSimT.ACC>(Wrk_PosSimT.PRE/2)) CLR(Val_Fdbk) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If Lock feedback is NOT used, because of Simulation or Configuration,
use sim timers to simulate locking and unlocking.

@@@@@  A timer is doubled to ensure it sets or clears the  @@@@@
@@@@@  .DN bit the same scan if the timer preset is zero.  @@@@@]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_UseLockFdbk) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) ][[XIC(Wrk_Lock) ,XIC(Wrk_Unlock) ] [TON(Wrk_LockSimT,?,?) TON(Wrk_LockSimT,?,?) ,CMP(Wrk_LockSimT.ACC>(Wrk_LockSimT.PRE/2)) OTU(Wrk_LockFdbk) OTU(Wrk_UnlockFdbk) ] ,XIC(Wrk_LockSimT.DN) [XIC(Wrk_Lock) OTL(Wrk_LockFdbk) ,XIC(Wrk_Unlock) OTL(Wrk_UnlockFdbk) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If Cylinder feedback is NOT used because of Configuration,
use sim timers to simulate the entend / left / retract / right or
extend / right / retract / left motion of the cylinders.

This is only needed when NOT in simulation; the logic above handles
simulation of position feedback, and cylinder simulation is not used.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Cfg_UseCylFdbk)XIO(Inp_Sim)[[XIC(Wrk_CylExtend) ,XIC(Wrk_CylRetract) ] [TON(Wrk_ExtRetrSimT,?,?) ,CMP(Wrk_ExtRetrSimT.ACC>(Wrk_ExtRetrSimT.PRE/2)) OTU(Wrk_CylExtFdbk) OTU(Wrk_CylRetrFdbk) ] ,XIC(Wrk_ExtRetrSimT.DN) [XIC(Wrk_CylExtend) OTL(Wrk_CylExtFdbk) ,XIC(Wrk_CylRetract) OTL(Wrk_CylRetrFdbk) ] ,[XIC(Wrk_CylLeft) ,XIC(Wrk_CylRight) ] [TON(Wrk_RightLeftSimT,?,?) ,CMP(Wrk_RightLeftSimT.ACC>(Wrk_RightLeftSimT.PRE/2)) OTU(Wrk_CylLeftFdbk) OTU(Wrk_CylRightFdbk) ] ,XIC(Wrk_RightLeftSimT.DN) [XIC(Wrk_CylLeft) OTL(Wrk_CylLeftFdbk) ,XIC(Wrk_CylRight) OTL(Wrk_CylRightFdbk) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Copy the last non-zero (confirmed) position of the device to a storage
register, used for figuring out which way to move toward target position.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LIM(1,Wrk_Fdbk,8)MOV(Wrk_Fdbk,Wrk_LastConfirmedPos);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
INTERLOCK / PERMISSIVE BYPASS / CHECK COMMAND HANDLING
============================================================
The Bypass Command bypasses the Bypassable Permissives and Interlocks.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(OCmd_Bypass)OTU(OCmd_Bypass)OTL(Wrk_Bypass);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Check Command enables checking of ALL
Permissives and Interlocks (cancels the bypass).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(OCmd_Check)OTU(OCmd_Check)OTU(Wrk_Bypass);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the internal Bypass flag is set, Bypassable Interlocks and Permissives ARE BYPASSED.
Bypassing is ACTIVE if Bypass selected OR in Maintenance Mode,
or in Override Mode if Override Bypassing is configured.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_Bypass) OTE(Sts_Bypass) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ,XIC(Sts_Ovrd) XIC(Cfg_OvrdPermIntlk) ]OTE(Sts_BypActive);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="19" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the internal Bypass flag is set, Bypassable Interlocks and Permissives ARE BYPASSED.
Bypassing is ACTIVE if Bypass selected OR in Maintenance Mode,
or in Override Mode if Override Bypassing is configured.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[[XIC(Inp_IntlkOK) ,XIC(Sts_BypActive) ] XIC(Inp_NBIntlkOK) OTE(Wrk_IntlkOK) ,[XIC(Inp_PermOK) ,XIC(Sts_BypActive) ] XIC(Inp_NBPermOK) OTE(Wrk_PermOK) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="20" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If a Maintenance Bypass function is active, display the Maintenance Bypass
Indicator (triangle symbol) on the graphic symbol.  Bypass functions are:
*  Interlock / Permissive Bypass function is enabled
*  Device HAS position feedback designated by engineer, but
maintenance has selected to NOT USE position feedback
*  Device HAS lock feedback designated by engineer, but
maintenance has selected to NOT USE lock feedback
*  Device HAS cylinder position feedback designated by engineer, but
maintenance has selected to NOT USE cylinder position feedback]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Sts_Bypass) ,XIC(Cfg_HasPosFdbk) XIO(Cfg_UsePosFdbk) ,XIC(Cfg_HasLockFdbk) XIO(Cfg_UseLockFdbk) ,XIC(Cfg_HasCylFdbk) XIO(Cfg_UseCylFdbk) ]OTE(Sts_MaintByp);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="21" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Ready for Interlock / Permissive Bypass if not bypassed.
Ready to cancel Bypass (resume checking) if bypassed.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Wrk_Bypass) OTE(Rdy_Bypass) ,XIC(Wrk_Bypass) OTE(Rdy_Check) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="22" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
DEVICE DISABLE/ENABLE COMMAND HANDLING
============================================================
The Disable Command disables the Analog Output.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MCmd_Disable)OTU(MCmd_Disable)XIC(Mode.Rdy_MRel)OTL(Wrk_Disabled);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="23" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Enable Command cancels the Disable and enables the Analog Output.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MCmd_Enable)OTU(MCmd_Enable)XIC(Mode.Rdy_MRel)OTU(Wrk_Disabled);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="24" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the internal Disabled flag is set, the valve is DISABLED.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_Disabled)OTE(Sts_Disabled);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="25" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Ready to Disable device if in Maintenance Mode and device is NOT Disabled.
Ready to Enable device if in Maintenance Mode and device IS Disabled.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mode.Rdy_MRel)[XIO(Wrk_Disabled) OTE(Rdy_Disable) ,XIC(Wrk_Disabled) OTE(Rdy_Enable) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="26" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ALARM RESET COMMAND HANDLING
============================================================
This rung handles the Alarm Reset Input and Commands
and the "Reset and Ack All" Operator Command.

This rung processes received Reset Commands from:

1.  The Operator via HMI Operator Command, or
2.  Higher-level strategies via Program Command
3.  Pushbuttons or other block via Input

and forwards the Reset to ALL Alarms and latched Shed conditions.

#####  V3.1-01  2014-08-29:  Corrections to Nrdy_ trip and reset logic.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_Reset) OTU(OCmd_Reset) ,XIC(OCmd_ResetAckAll) OTU(OCmd_ResetAckAll) [OTL(PCmd_PosFailAck) ,OTL(PCmd_LockFailAck) ,OTL(PCmd_IntlkTripAck) ,OTL(PCmd_IOFaultAck) ] ,XIC(PCmd_Reset) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_Reset) ,NOP() ] ,XIC(Inp_Reset) ][OTU(Wrk_PosFailSts) OTU(Wrk_LockFailSts) ,OTL(PosFail.PCmd_Reset) OTL(LockFail.PCmd_Reset) ,OTL(IntlkTrip.PCmd_Reset) OTL(IOFault.PCmd_Reset) ,OTE(Wrk_FaultRes) ,[XIO(Inp_IOFault) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) ] OTU(Nrdy_IOFault) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="27" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Device is NOT READY if:

* Interlocks are not OK (accounting for bypassing)
* Permissives are not OK (accounting for bypassing)
* There is an I/O Fault and the device is not in Simulation
* The Device has a Position Fail or Lock Fail that has not been reset
* The Device is disabled.
* The Device has a configuration error

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx).  #####
#####  V3.1-01  2014-08-29:  Corrections to Nrdy_ trip and reset logic.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_State,6)OTE(Nrdy_Fail);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="28" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Device is NOT READY if:

* Interlocks are not OK (accounting for bypassing)
* Permissives are not OK (accounting for bypassing)
* There is an I/O Fault and the device is not in Simulation
* The Device has a Position Fail or Lock Fail that has not been reset
* The Device is disabled.
* The Device has a configuration error

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx).  #####
#####  V3.1-01  2014-08-29:  Corrections to Nrdy_ trip and reset logic.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Nrdy_NoMode)[XIC(Sts_Disabled) OTE(Nrdy_Disabled) ,XIC(Sts_Err) OTE(Nrdy_CfgErr) ,XIO(Wrk_IntlkOK) [NEQ(Wrk_Cmd,1) OTE(Sts_IntlkTrip) ,OTE(Nrdy_Intlk) ] ,XIO(Wrk_PermOK) OTE(Nrdy_Perm) ,XIC(Inp_IOFault) XIO(Inp_Sim) OTE(Sts_IOFault) XIC(Cfg_ShedOnIOFault) OTL(Nrdy_IOFault) ]OTE(Wrk_NotRdy);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="29" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Device is NOT READY if:

* Interlocks are not OK (accounting for bypassing)
* Permissives are not OK (accounting for bypassing)
* There is an I/O Fault and the device is not in Simulation
* The Device has a Position Fail or Lock Fail that has not been reset
* The Device is disabled.
* The Device has a configuration error

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx).  #####
#####  V3.1-01  2014-08-29:  Corrections to Nrdy_ trip and reset logic.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_NotRdy) ,XIC(Nrdy_Fail) ,XIC(Nrdy_IOFault) ]OTE(Sts_NotRdy);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="30" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Device is AVAILABLE for automation if it is in PROGRAM
Mode and the "Not Ready" status is cleared.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Sts_Prog)XIO(Sts_NotRdy)OTE(Sts_Available);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="31" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
HANDLE POSITION COMMANDS
============================================================
If a valid Positioin 1 Command is received (in Oper, Maint or Prog), or an
Override to Position 1 is received, or the device is in Position 1 in Hand Mode,
set the commanded position to 1.  Flag if this is a NEW commanded position.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_Pos1) OTU(OCmd_Pos1) [XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] ,XIC(PCmd_Pos1) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_Pos1) ,NOP() ] XIC(Sts_Prog) ,EQU(Inp_OvrdCmd,1) CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd) XIC(Sts_Ovrd) ]XIC(Wrk_PermOK)XIC(Wrk_IntlkOK)[XIC(Cfg_CmdDuringMove) NEQ(Wrk_Cmd,1) ,EQU(Wrk_Cmd,0) ][NEQ(Wrk_State,1) ,NEQ(Wrk_Fdbk,1) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ]OTL(Wrk_NewCmd)MOV(1,Wrk_Cmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="32" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If a valid Positioin 2 Command is received (in Oper, Maint or Prog), or an
Override to Position 2 is received, or the device is in Position 2 in Hand Mode,
set the commanded position to 2.  Flag if this is a NEW commanded position.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_Pos2) OTU(OCmd_Pos2) [XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] ,XIC(PCmd_Pos2) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_Pos2) ,NOP() ] XIC(Sts_Prog) ,EQU(Inp_OvrdCmd,2) CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd) XIC(Sts_Ovrd) ]GEQ(Cfg_NumPos,2)XIC(Wrk_PermOK)XIC(Wrk_IntlkOK)[XIC(Cfg_CmdDuringMove) NEQ(Wrk_Cmd,2) ,EQU(Wrk_Cmd,0) ][NEQ(Wrk_State,1) ,NEQ(Wrk_Fdbk,2) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ,XIC(Cfg_ViaPos1) ]OTL(Wrk_NewCmd)MOV(2,Wrk_Cmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="33" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If a valid Positioin 3 Command is received (in Oper, Maint or Prog), or an
Override to Position 3 is received, or the device is in Position 3 in Hand Mode,
set the commanded position to 3.  Flag if this is a NEW commanded position.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_Pos3) OTU(OCmd_Pos3) [XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] ,XIC(PCmd_Pos3) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_Pos3) ,NOP() ] XIC(Sts_Prog) ,EQU(Inp_OvrdCmd,3) CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd) XIC(Sts_Ovrd) ]GEQ(Cfg_NumPos,3)XIC(Wrk_PermOK)XIC(Wrk_IntlkOK)[XIC(Cfg_CmdDuringMove) NEQ(Wrk_Cmd,3) ,EQU(Wrk_Cmd,0) ][NEQ(Wrk_State,1) ,NEQ(Wrk_Fdbk,3) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ,XIC(Cfg_ViaPos1) ]OTL(Wrk_NewCmd)MOV(3,Wrk_Cmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="34" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If a valid Positioin 4 Command is received (in Oper, Maint or Prog), or an
Override to Position 4 is received, or the device is in Position 4 in Hand Mode,
set the commanded position to 4.  Flag if this is a NEW commanded position.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_Pos4) OTU(OCmd_Pos4) [XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] ,XIC(PCmd_Pos4) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_Pos4) ,NOP() ] XIC(Sts_Prog) ,EQU(Inp_OvrdCmd,4) CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd) XIC(Sts_Ovrd) ]GEQ(Cfg_NumPos,4)XIC(Wrk_PermOK)XIC(Wrk_IntlkOK)[XIC(Cfg_CmdDuringMove) NEQ(Wrk_Cmd,4) ,EQU(Wrk_Cmd,0) ][NEQ(Wrk_State,1) ,NEQ(Wrk_Fdbk,4) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ,XIC(Cfg_ViaPos1) ]OTL(Wrk_NewCmd)MOV(4,Wrk_Cmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="35" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If a valid Positioin 5 Command is received (in Oper, Maint or Prog), or an
Override to Position 5 is received, or the device is in Position 5 in Hand Mode,
set the commanded position to 5.  Flag if this is a NEW commanded position.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_Pos5) OTU(OCmd_Pos5) [XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] ,XIC(PCmd_Pos5) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_Pos5) ,NOP() ] XIC(Sts_Prog) ,EQU(Inp_OvrdCmd,5) CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd) XIC(Sts_Ovrd) ]GEQ(Cfg_NumPos,5)XIC(Wrk_PermOK)XIC(Wrk_IntlkOK)[XIC(Cfg_CmdDuringMove) NEQ(Wrk_Cmd,5) ,EQU(Wrk_Cmd,0) ][NEQ(Wrk_State,1) ,NEQ(Wrk_Fdbk,5) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ,XIC(Cfg_ViaPos1) ]OTL(Wrk_NewCmd)MOV(5,Wrk_Cmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="36" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If a valid Positioin 6 Command is received (in Oper, Maint or Prog), or an
Override to Position 6 is received, or the device is in Position 6 in Hand Mode,
set the commanded position to 6.  Flag if this is a NEW commanded position.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_Pos6) OTU(OCmd_Pos6) [XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] ,XIC(PCmd_Pos6) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_Pos6) ,NOP() ] XIC(Sts_Prog) ,EQU(Inp_OvrdCmd,6) CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd) XIC(Sts_Ovrd) ]GEQ(Cfg_NumPos,6)XIC(Wrk_PermOK)XIC(Wrk_IntlkOK)[XIC(Cfg_CmdDuringMove) NEQ(Wrk_Cmd,6) ,EQU(Wrk_Cmd,0) ][NEQ(Wrk_State,1) ,NEQ(Wrk_Fdbk,6) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ,XIC(Cfg_ViaPos1) ]OTL(Wrk_NewCmd)MOV(6,Wrk_Cmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="37" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If a valid Positioin 7 Command is received (in Oper, Maint or Prog), or an
Override to Position 7 is received, or the device is in Position 7 in Hand Mode,
set the commanded position to 7.  Flag if this is a NEW commanded position.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_Pos7) OTU(OCmd_Pos7) [XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] ,XIC(PCmd_Pos7) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_Pos7) ,NOP() ] XIC(Sts_Prog) ,EQU(Inp_OvrdCmd,7) CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd) XIC(Sts_Ovrd) ]GEQ(Cfg_NumPos,7)XIC(Wrk_PermOK)XIC(Wrk_IntlkOK)[XIC(Cfg_CmdDuringMove) NEQ(Wrk_Cmd,7) ,EQU(Wrk_Cmd,0) ][NEQ(Wrk_State,1) ,NEQ(Wrk_Fdbk,7) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ,XIC(Cfg_ViaPos1) ]OTL(Wrk_NewCmd)MOV(7,Wrk_Cmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="38" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If a valid Position 8 Command is received (in Oper, Maint or Prog), or an
Override to Position 8 is received, or the device is in Position 8 in Hand Mode,
set the commanded position to 8.  Flag if this is a NEW commanded position.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_Pos8) OTU(OCmd_Pos8) [XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] ,XIC(PCmd_Pos8) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_Pos8) ,NOP() ] XIC(Sts_Prog) ,EQU(Inp_OvrdCmd,8) CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd) XIC(Sts_Ovrd) ]GEQ(Cfg_NumPos,8)XIC(Wrk_PermOK)XIC(Wrk_IntlkOK)[XIC(Cfg_CmdDuringMove) NEQ(Wrk_Cmd,8) ,EQU(Wrk_Cmd,0) ][NEQ(Wrk_State,1) ,NEQ(Wrk_Fdbk,8) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ,XIC(Cfg_ViaPos1) ]OTL(Wrk_NewCmd)MOV(8,Wrk_Cmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="39" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Device is configured to GO TO POSITION 1 ON INTERLOCK OR FAULT, 
then if an Interlock that is not bypassed is NOT OK, or if the Device is disabled or
faulted, send the Device to position 1.  If an interlock not OK caused the Device Target Position
to CHANGE to POSITION 1, show an Interlock Trip status (and possibly alarm).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_IntlkToPos1)XIC(Sts_NotRdy)NEQ(Wrk_Cmd,1)[NEQ(Wrk_State,1) ,NEQ(Wrk_Fdbk,1) ]OTL(Wrk_NewCmd)MOV(1,Wrk_Cmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="40" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_NewCmd)MOV(Wrk_Cmd,Wrk_LastCmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="41" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
DEVICE STATE MACHINE
============================================================
The following rungs control device motion through a set of states.
0 = Reset / Unknown and awaiting command
1 = In Position and Locked
2 = Unlocking
3 = Moving to Position 1 (retry)
4 = Movition to Target Position
5 = Locking
6 = Faulted
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
POWERUP
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
On Powerup:
* If the device is in simulation:
- if the current position is valid, copy it to the target position and go to State 1 (Locked In Position)
- if the current position is invalid, go to State 6 (Faulted)
* If the device is NOT in simulation:
- if the device ]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(S:FS) ,XIC(Sts_Hand) ]OTU(Wrk_NewCmd)CLR(Wrk_Cmd)CLR(Wrk_LastCmd)[XIC(Cfg_HasPosFdbk) LIM(1,Wrk_Fdbk,8) MOV(Wrk_Fdbk,Wrk_LastCmd) [[XIC(Wrk_LockFdbk) ,XIO(Cfg_HasLock) ] JMP(State1) ,MOV(Wrk_Fdbk,Wrk_Cmd) RES(Wrk_LockChkT) JMP(State5) ] ,JMP(State0) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="42" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx).  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Nrdy_IOFault)JMP(State6);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="43" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If not powerup, based on the current state, jump to the code for that state.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(S:FS)[EQU(Wrk_State,1) JMP(State1) ,EQU(Wrk_State,2) JMP(State2) ,EQU(Wrk_State,3) JMP(State3) ,EQU(Wrk_State,4) JMP(State4) ,EQU(Wrk_State,5) JMP(State5) ,EQU(Wrk_State,6) JMP(State6) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="44" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
STATE 0 : RESET / UNKNOWN, AWAITING COMMAND
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Actions in State 0:
* Show current state as 0
* Turn off the Position Increase and Decrease outputs
* Leave the Lock and Unlock outputs in their last states]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(State0)[MOV(0,Wrk_State) CLR(Wrk_RetryC) ,OTU(Wrk_Inc) OTU(Wrk_Dec) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="45" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Transitions out of State 0 (Reset / Unknown)
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
If a new position is commanded, go to State 2 (Unlocking).

(Note on style: in this state machine, we reset the timer used int the NEXT
step on the transition INTO THAT STEP  ---  on these branches).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_NewCmd)OTU(Wrk_NewCmd)RES(Wrk_UnlockChkT)CLR(Wrk_RetryC)JMP(State2);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="46" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[JMP(Outputs);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="47" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
STATE 1: IN POSITION
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Actions in State 1:
* Show current state as 1
* Clear the Retry Count
* Turn off the Position Increase and Decrease outputs and the Unlock output,
and if the device is not in Simulation, energize the Lock output]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(State1)[MOV(1,Wrk_State) CLR(Wrk_RetryC) ,OTU(Wrk_Inc) OTU(Wrk_Dec) OTU(Wrk_Lock) OTU(Wrk_Unlock) ,XIC(Cfg_HasLock) OTL(Wrk_Lock) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="48" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Transitions out of State 1 (In Position)
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
If a new position is commanded, go to State 2 (Unlocking).
If the device moves out of position, flag a Position Failure (with Alarm),
or if the device lock confirmation is lost, flag a Lock Failure (with Alarm).
In either of these last two cases, go to State 6 (Faulted).

(Note on style: in this state machine, we reset the timer used int the NEXT
step on the transition INTO THAT STEP  ---  on these branches).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_NewCmd) OTU(Wrk_NewCmd) RES(Wrk_UnlockChkT) CLR(Wrk_RetryC) JMP(State2) ,NEQ(Wrk_Fdbk,Wrk_LastCmd) OTL(Wrk_PosFailSts) XIC(Cfg_ShedOnPosFail) OTL(Wrk_PosFail) JMP(State6) ,XIC(Cfg_HasLock) [XIO(Wrk_LockFdbk) ,XIC(Wrk_UnlockFdbk) ] OTL(Wrk_LockFailSts) XIC(Cfg_ShedOnLockFail) OTL(Wrk_LockFail) JMP(State6) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="49" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[JMP(Outputs);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="50" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
STATE 2: UNLOCKING
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Actions in State 2:
* Show current state as 2
* Turn off the Position Increase and Decrease outputs and the Lock output,
and if the device has a lock and is not in Simulation, energize the Unlock output]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(State2)[MOV(2,Wrk_State) TON(Wrk_UnlockChkT,?,?) ,OTU(Wrk_Inc) OTU(Wrk_Dec) OTU(Wrk_Lock) OTU(Wrk_Unlock) ,XIC(Cfg_HasLock) OTL(Wrk_Unlock) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="51" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Transitions out of State 2 (Unlocking)
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
If unlocking has been confirmed (or the device has no locking),
go to State 3 if the device must move via Position 1 and it is not there already,
or go to State 4 to go directly to the target position.

If the Unlock Check timer times out, we were not able to unlock the device.
Flag the Lock Failure (and alarm) and go to State 6 (Faulted).

(Note on style: in this state machine, we reset the timer used int the NEXT
step on the transition INTO THAT STEP  ---  on these branches).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[[XIC(Wrk_UnlockFdbk) ,XIO(Cfg_HasLock) ] OTU(Wrk_Unlock) RES(Wrk_VerifyT) [XIC(Cfg_ViaPos1) NEQ(Wrk_Fdbk,1) RES(Wrk_Pos1ChkT) JMP(State3) ,RES(Wrk_PosChkT) JMP(State4) ] ,XIC(Wrk_UnlockChkT.DN) OTL(Wrk_LockFailSts) XIC(Cfg_ShedOnLockFail) OTL(Wrk_LockFail) JMP(State6) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="52" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[JMP(Outputs);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="53" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
STATE 3: MOVING TO POSITION 1
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Actions in State 3:
* Show current state as 3
* Turn off the Position Increase output and the Lock output;
if the device is not in Simulation, energize the Position Decrease outout,
and if the device is not in Simulation and has a lock, energize the Unlock output
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(State3)[MOV(3,Wrk_State) TON(Wrk_Pos1ChkT,?,?) ,OTU(Wrk_Inc) OTU(Wrk_Dec) OTU(Wrk_Lock) OTU(Wrk_Unlock) ,[XIC(Cfg_HasLock) OTL(Wrk_Unlock) ,NEQ(Wrk_Fdbk,1) OTL(Wrk_Dec) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="54" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Transitions out of State 3 (Moving to Position 1)
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
If we reach position 1, stop motion and start a verify timer
If the device is still in position 1 when the verify time is complete
(doesn't coast past), go to State 4 (Moving to Commanded Position).

If the Position 1 Check timer expires or if the Verify timer expires and the device is
NOT in position 1, raise a Position Fail and go to State 6 (Faulted).

If we are moving to position 1 and the device becomes Locked
(or confirmation of Unlocked is lost), raise a Lock Fail and go to State 6 (Faulted).

@@@@@  A timer is doubled to ensure it sets or clears the  @@@@@
@@@@@  .DN bit the same scan if the timer preset is zero.  @@@@@]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[[EQU(Wrk_Fdbk,1) ,XIC(Wrk_VerifyT.TT) ] OTU(Wrk_Dec) TON(Wrk_VerifyT,?,?) TON(Wrk_VerifyT,?,?) ,[XIC(Wrk_VerifyT.DN) EQU(Wrk_Fdbk,1) ,XIO(Cfg_ViaPos1) ] RES(Wrk_PosChkT) RES(Wrk_VerifyT) JMP(State4) ,[XIC(Wrk_Pos1ChkT.DN) ,XIC(Wrk_VerifyT.DN) ] OTL(Wrk_PosFailSts) XIC(Cfg_ShedOnPosFail) OTL(Wrk_PosFail) JMP(State6) ,XIC(Cfg_HasLock) [XIC(Wrk_LockFdbk) ,XIO(Wrk_UnlockFdbk) ] OTL(Wrk_LockFailSts) XIC(Cfg_ShedOnLockFail) OTL(Wrk_LockFail) JMP(State6) ,XIC(Wrk_NewCmd) OTU(Wrk_NewCmd) RES(Wrk_UnlockChkT) CLR(Wrk_RetryC) JMP(State2) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="55" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[JMP(Outputs);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="56" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
STATE 4: MOVING TO COMMANDED POSITION
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Actions in State 4:
* Show current state as 4
* Turn off the Lock output;
* If the device is not in Simulation and has a lock, energize the Unlock output.
* If the device is not in Simulation, move in the appropriate direction until
the commanded position is reached:

-- circular and NOT clockwise only:  shortest path around circle

-- circular and clockwise only:  increase

-- NOT circular and NOT via position 1:
---- if cmd position < current position - decrease
---- if cmd position > current position - increase

-- NOT circular and via position 1:
---- we're in position  1, so increase]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(State4)[MOV(4,Wrk_State) TON(Wrk_PosChkT,?,?) ,OTU(Wrk_Inc) OTU(Wrk_Dec) OTU(Wrk_Lock) OTU(Wrk_Unlock) ,XIC(Cfg_HasLock) OTL(Wrk_Unlock) ,NEQ(Wrk_Fdbk,Wrk_Cmd) [XIC(Cfg_Circ) XIO(Cfg_CWOnly) [ONS(Wrk_CalcONS) CPT(Wrk_PosAway,(Wrk_Cmd-Wrk_Fdbk+Cfg_NumPos)MOD Cfg_NumPos) ,CMP(Wrk_PosAway>(Cfg_NumPos/2)) OTL(Wrk_Dec) ,CMP(Wrk_PosAway<=(Cfg_NumPos/2)) OTL(Wrk_Inc) ] ,[XIC(Cfg_CWOnly) ,XIC(Cfg_ViaPos1) ] OTL(Wrk_Inc) ,XIO(Cfg_Circ) XIO(Cfg_ViaPos1) [GRT(Wrk_Cmd,Wrk_LastConfirmedPos) OTL(Wrk_Inc) ,LES(Wrk_Cmd,Wrk_LastConfirmedPos) OTL(Wrk_Dec) ] ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="57" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Transitions out of State 4 (Moving to Commanded Position)
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
If we reach the commanded position, stop motion and start a verify timer
If the device is still in the commanded position when the verify time is complete
(doesn't coast past), go to State 5 (Locking).

If the Position Check timer expires or if the Verify timer expires and the device is
NOT in the commanded position,  if retries are available and we are moving
via position 1, go back to state 3 and retry the move.  If no retries are
available or we don't move via position 1, we can't retry the move, so
raise a Position Fail and go to State 6 (Faulted).

If we are moving to the commanded position and the device becomes Locked
(or confirmation of Unlocked is lost), raise a Lock Fail and go to State 6 (Faulted).

@@@@@  A timer is doubled to ensure it sets or clears the  @@@@@
@@@@@  .DN bit the same scan if the timer preset is zero.  @@@@@]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[[EQU(Wrk_Fdbk,Wrk_Cmd) ,XIC(Wrk_VerifyT.TT) ] OTU(Wrk_Inc) OTU(Wrk_Dec) TON(Wrk_VerifyT,?,?) TON(Wrk_VerifyT,?,?) ,XIC(Wrk_VerifyT.DN) EQU(Wrk_Fdbk,Wrk_Cmd) RES(Wrk_LockChkT) JMP(State5) ,[XIC(Wrk_PosChkT.DN) ,XIC(Wrk_VerifyT.DN) ] [XIC(Cfg_ViaPos1) LES(Wrk_RetryC,Cfg_Retries) ADD(Wrk_RetryC,1,Wrk_RetryC) RES(Wrk_Pos1ChkT) RES(Wrk_VerifyT) JMP(State3) ,OTL(Wrk_PosFailSts) XIC(Cfg_ShedOnPosFail) OTL(Wrk_PosFail) JMP(State6) ] ,XIC(Cfg_HasLock) [XIC(Wrk_LockFdbk) ,XIO(Wrk_UnlockFdbk) ] OTL(Wrk_LockFailSts) XIC(Cfg_ShedOnLockFail) OTL(Wrk_LockFail) JMP(State6) ,XIC(Wrk_NewCmd) OTU(Wrk_NewCmd) RES(Wrk_UnlockChkT) CLR(Wrk_RetryC) JMP(State2) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="58" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[JMP(Outputs);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="59" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
STATE 5: LOCKING
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Actions in State 5:
* Show current state as 5
* Turn off the Position Increase and Decrease outputs and the Unlock output,
and if the device has a lock and is not in Simulation, energize the Lock output]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(State5)[MOV(5,Wrk_State) ,OTU(Wrk_Inc) OTU(Wrk_Dec) OTU(Wrk_Lock) OTU(Wrk_Unlock) ,XIC(Cfg_HasLock) OTL(Wrk_Lock) ,TON(Wrk_LockChkT,?,?) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="60" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Transitions out of State 5 (Locking)
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
If locking has been confirmed (or the device has no locking), go to State 1
(in position and locked).

If the device moves out of position before the locking is complete,
then if the device can retry via position 1, do so (State 3, Moving to Pos. 1).
Otherwise, flag the position fault (and alarm) and go to State 6 (Faulted).

If the Lock Check timer times out, we were not able to lock the device.
Flag the Lock Failure (and alarm) and go to State 6 (Faulted).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[[XIC(Wrk_LockFdbk) ,XIO(Cfg_HasLock) ] OTU(Wrk_Lock) CLR(Wrk_Cmd) JMP(State1) ,NEQ(Wrk_Fdbk,Wrk_Cmd) [XIC(Cfg_ViaPos1) LES(Wrk_RetryC,Cfg_Retries) ADD(Wrk_RetryC,1,Wrk_RetryC) JMP(State3) ,OTL(Wrk_PosFailSts) XIC(Cfg_ShedOnPosFail) OTL(Wrk_PosFail) JMP(State6) ] ,XIC(Wrk_LockChkT.DN) OTL(Wrk_LockFailSts) XIC(Cfg_ShedOnLockFail) OTL(Wrk_LockFail) JMP(State6) ,XIC(Wrk_NewCmd) OTU(Wrk_NewCmd) RES(Wrk_UnlockChkT) CLR(Wrk_RetryC) JMP(State2) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="61" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[JMP(Outputs);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="62" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
STATE 6: FAULTED
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Actions in State 6:
* Show current state as 6
* Turn off the Position Increase and Decrease outputs and the Lock and Unlock outputs
* Wait for Fault Reset]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(State6)[MOV(6,Wrk_State) ,OTU(Wrk_Inc) OTU(Wrk_Dec) OTU(Wrk_Lock) OTU(Wrk_Unlock) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="63" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Transitions out of State 6 (Faulted)
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
If a reset is received, then:

If the device is not in the commanded position, go to State 2 (Unlocking)

If the device is in the commanded position and locked, go to State 1 (In Position and Locked)

If the device is in the commanded position and NOT locked, go to State 5 (Locking)

(Fail status bits and alarm input bits are cleared on the Reset command rung.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_FaultRes) [LIM(1,Wrk_Fdbk,8) MOV(Wrk_Fdbk,Wrk_LastCmd) [[XIC(Wrk_LockFdbk) ,XIO(Cfg_HasLock) ] JMP(State1) ,RES(Wrk_LockChkT) JMP(State5) ] ,JMP(State0) ] ,XIC(Wrk_NewCmd) OTU(Wrk_NewCmd) XIC(Cfg_OCmdResets) [XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] RES(Wrk_UnlockChkT) CLR(Wrk_RetryC) JMP(State2) ,CLR(Wrk_Cmd) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="64" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the device is NOT Faulted (on a fault reset), clear the latched faults.
If the device is OK and Idle (not executing a move), clear the alarm inputs
for Position Fail and Lock Fail.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx).  #####
#####  V3.1-01  2014-09-03:  Fixed Not Ready resets.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(Outputs)[NEQ(Wrk_State,6) OTU(Wrk_PosFail) OTU(Wrk_LockFail) ,EQU(Wrk_State,1) OTU(Wrk_PosFailSts) OTU(Wrk_LockFailSts) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="65" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
OUTPUT PROCESSING
============================================================
OUTPUTS:  Outputs to move cylinders for an n-Position RTSV
to "walk" the diverter to the new position.
(Counter-Clockwise -- Decrease -- = Extend, right, retract, left, etc.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_Dec)XIO(Inp_Sim)[[XIC(Wrk_CylLeftFdbk) ,XIC(Wrk_CCWRetr) ] XIO(Wrk_CylRightFdbk) OTE(Wrk_CCWRetr) ,XIC(Wrk_CylRetrFdbk) XIO(Wrk_CylExtFdbk) OTE(Wrk_CCWRight) ,[XIC(Wrk_CylRightFdbk) ,XIC(Wrk_CCWExt) ] XIO(Wrk_CylLeftFdbk) OTE(Wrk_CCWExt) ,XIC(Wrk_CylExtFdbk) XIO(Wrk_CylLeftFdbk) OTE(Wrk_CCWLeft) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="66" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[OUTPUTS:  Outputs to move cylinders for an n-Position RTSV
to "walk" the diverter to the new position.
(Clockwise -- Increase --  = extend, left, retract, right, etc.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_Inc)XIO(Inp_Sim)[[XIC(Wrk_CylRightFdbk) ,XIC(Wrk_CWRetr) ] XIO(Wrk_CylLeftFdbk) OTE(Wrk_CWRetr) ,XIC(Wrk_CylRetrFdbk) XIO(Wrk_CylExtFdbk) OTE(Wrk_CWLeft) ,[XIC(Wrk_CylLeftFdbk) ,XIC(Wrk_CWExt) ] XIO(Wrk_CylRightFdbk) OTE(Wrk_CWExt) ,XIC(Wrk_CylExtFdbk) XIO(Wrk_CylRetrFdbk) OTE(Wrk_CWRight) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="67" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[OUTPUTS: Collect above requests into outputs to RTSV stepping cylinders.
Energize the physical outputs if the Device is not in Simulation.
Note the Extend output is delayed by a configurable time.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_CCWExt) ,XIC(Wrk_CWExt) ]TON(Wrk_ExtendT,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="68" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[These rungs set the outputs for the RTSV stepping cylinders.
Work bits are set for the device simulation, and if the device is
NOT in simulation, the hardware outputs are set.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_ExtendT.DN)[OTE(Wrk_CylExtend) ,XIO(Inp_Sim) OTE(Out_CylExtend) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="69" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_CCWRight) ,XIC(Wrk_CWRight) ][OTE(Wrk_CylRight) ,XIO(Inp_Sim) OTE(Out_CylRight) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="70" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_CCWRetr) ,XIC(Wrk_CWRetr) ][OTE(Wrk_CylRetract) ,XIO(Inp_Sim) OTE(Out_CylRetract) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="71" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_CCWLeft) ,XIC(Wrk_CWLeft) ][OTE(Wrk_CylLeft) ,XIO(Inp_Sim) OTE(Out_CylLeft) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="72" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If we are telling the physical (not simulated) Device to move,
set the appropriate Increment or Decrement Output and the target
Position Output.  (The latter is latched in if not cleared on the rung below.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Inp_Sim)[XIC(Wrk_Inc) OTE(Out_Inc) ,XIC(Wrk_Dec) OTE(Out_Dec) ,XIC(Cfg_OutPosLatch) ][EQU(Wrk_State,3) MOV(1,Wrk_Out) ,EQU(Wrk_State,4) [CLR(Wrk_Out) ,EQU(Wrk_Cmd,1) OTL(Wrk_Out.0) ,EQU(Wrk_Cmd,2) OTL(Wrk_Out.1) ,EQU(Wrk_Cmd,3) OTL(Wrk_Out.2) ,EQU(Wrk_Cmd,4) OTL(Wrk_Out.3) ,EQU(Wrk_Cmd,5) OTL(Wrk_Out.4) ,EQU(Wrk_Cmd,6) OTL(Wrk_Out.5) ,EQU(Wrk_Cmd,7) OTL(Wrk_Out.6) ,EQU(Wrk_Cmd,8) OTL(Wrk_Out.7) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="73" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Clear the Position Outputs if the Device is Faulted or in Simulation, or if
no motion is required and Output Position Latching is disabled.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[EQU(Wrk_State,6) ,XIO(Wrk_Inc) XIO(Wrk_Dec) XIO(Cfg_OutPosLatch) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) ]CLR(Wrk_Out);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="74" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung copies the buffered output bits to the actual outputs.

(NOTE:  These are copeid rather than aliased because the Wrk_Out bits are
only written as needed.  Buffering keeps writes to Out_Pos1, etc., from
affecting the internal state of the instruction instance.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_Out.0) OTE(Out_Pos1) ,XIC(Wrk_Out.1) OTE(Out_Pos2) ,XIC(Wrk_Out.2) OTE(Out_Pos3) ,XIC(Wrk_Out.3) OTE(Out_Pos4) ,XIC(Wrk_Out.4) OTE(Out_Pos5) ,XIC(Wrk_Out.5) OTE(Out_Pos6) ,XIC(Wrk_Out.6) OTE(Out_Pos7) ,XIC(Wrk_Out.7) OTE(Out_Pos8) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="75" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Device is not in Simulation, energize the Lock and Unlock outputs as requested above.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Inp_Sim)[XIC(Wrk_Lock) OTE(Out_Lock) ,XIC(Wrk_Unlock) OTE(Out_Unlock) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="76" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
OTHER VALUES
============================================================
This rung generates values not generated above:
Commanded (target) Position
State Machine current state (for HMI animation)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(Wrk_Cmd,Val_Cmd)MOV(Wrk_State,Val_State);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="77" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Val_Sts is the current device status, as determined by this AOI,
based on its knowledge of commands executed and feedback.
(This is the status that should be monitored by, for example, FT Historian.)
0 = Powerup / Unknown (Hand Mode with no feedback, for example)
1 = Position 1
2 = Position 2
3 = Position 3
4 = Position 4
5 = Position 5
6 = Position 6
7 = Position 7
8 = Position 8
9 = Moving
33 = Device Disabled

Val_Fault is the current device fault status, as determined by this AOI,
based on its knowledge of commands executed and feedback.
(This is the fault status that should be monitored by, for example, FT Historian.)
0 = None
16 = Position Failure
17 = Lock Failure
32 = I/O Fault
34 = Configuration Error]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_Sts) CLR(Wrk_Fault) ,EQU(Wrk_State,1) MOV(Wrk_Fdbk,Wrk_Sts) ,LIM(2,Wrk_State,5) MOV(9,Wrk_Sts) ,XIC(Wrk_PosFailSts) MOV(16,Wrk_Fault) ,XIC(Wrk_LockFailSts) MOV(17,Wrk_Fault) ,XIC(Sts_IOFault) MOV(32,Wrk_Fault) ,XIC(Sts_Disabled) MOV(33,Wrk_Sts) ,XIC(Sts_Err) MOV(34,Wrk_Fault) ,MOV(Wrk_Sts,Val_Sts) MOV(Wrk_Fault,Val_Fault) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="78" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung copies the buffered failure status bits to the actual Status output parameters.

(NOTE:  These are copeid rather than aliased because the Wrk_xxxFailSts bits are
only written as needed.  Buffering keeps writes to Sts_PosFail and Sts_LockFail
from affecting the internal state of the instruction instance.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_PosFailSts) OTE(Sts_PosFail) ,XIC(Wrk_LockFailSts) OTE(Sts_LockFail) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="79" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung generates the Device Position Status bits.
If the Device has ACHIEVED THE TARGET POSITION
(it has reached a state and that state is the Target State),
then show the position; otherwise, the Device is MOVING.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[EQU(Wrk_Fdbk,Wrk_LastCmd) [EQU(Wrk_Fdbk,1) OTE(Sts_Pos1) ,EQU(Wrk_Fdbk,2) OTE(Sts_Pos2) ,EQU(Wrk_Fdbk,3) OTE(Sts_Pos3) ,EQU(Wrk_Fdbk,4) OTE(Sts_Pos4) ,EQU(Wrk_Fdbk,5) OTE(Sts_Pos5) ,EQU(Wrk_Fdbk,6) OTE(Sts_Pos6) ,EQU(Wrk_Fdbk,7) OTE(Sts_Pos7) ,EQU(Wrk_Fdbk,8) OTE(Sts_Pos8) ] ,LIM(2,Wrk_State,5) OTE(Sts_Moving) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="80" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ENUMERATED SOURCE / QUALITY VALUES
============================================================
Source and Quality for Input / Output values / status (SrcQ_IO)

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Inp_IOFault) MOV(34,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) MOV(9,Wrk_SrcQ) ,MOV(Wrk_SrcQ,SrcQ_IO) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="81" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Source and Quality for primary values / status (SrcQ)

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(SrcQ_IO,SrcQ);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="82" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
OPERATOR COMMAND READIES
============================================================
This rung sets up a work bit to simplify the next rung by reducing repeated logic.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[NEQ(Wrk_State,1) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) XIO(Cfg_OutPosLatch) ]OTE(Wrk_MaintTrig);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="83" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Generally, that Device is ready for a new state command if it is not already targeted
at that state, if the permissives and interlocks (subject to bypassing) allow it,
the Device is in Operator or Maintenance Mode, and the Device is not
disabled or faulted.

#####  V3.1-01  2014-08-29:  Corrections to Nrdy_ trip and reset logic.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ]XIO(Wrk_NotRdy)[XIO(Sts_NotRdy) ,XIC(Cfg_OCmdResets) ][EQU(Wrk_Cmd,0) ,XIC(Cfg_CmdDuringMove) ][NEQ(Wrk_Cmd,1) [XIC(Wrk_MaintTrig) ,NEQ(Wrk_Fdbk,1) ] OTE(Rdy_Pos1) ,NEQ(Wrk_Cmd,2) [XIC(Wrk_MaintTrig) ,XIC(Cfg_ViaPos1) ,NEQ(Wrk_Fdbk,2) ] OTE(Rdy_Pos2) ,GEQ(Cfg_NumPos,3) NEQ(Wrk_Cmd,3) [XIC(Wrk_MaintTrig) ,XIC(Cfg_ViaPos1) ,NEQ(Wrk_Fdbk,3) ] OTE(Rdy_Pos3) ,GEQ(Cfg_NumPos,4) NEQ(Wrk_Cmd,4) [XIC(Wrk_MaintTrig) ,XIC(Cfg_ViaPos1) ,NEQ(Wrk_Fdbk,4) ] OTE(Rdy_Pos4) ,GEQ(Cfg_NumPos,5) NEQ(Wrk_Cmd,5) [XIC(Wrk_MaintTrig) ,XIC(Cfg_ViaPos1) ,NEQ(Wrk_Fdbk,5) ] OTE(Rdy_Pos5) ,GEQ(Cfg_NumPos,6) NEQ(Wrk_Cmd,6) [XIC(Wrk_MaintTrig) ,XIC(Cfg_ViaPos1) ,NEQ(Wrk_Fdbk,6) ] OTE(Rdy_Pos6) ,GEQ(Cfg_NumPos,7) NEQ(Wrk_Cmd,7) [XIC(Wrk_MaintTrig) ,XIC(Cfg_ViaPos1) ,NEQ(Wrk_Fdbk,7) ] OTE(Rdy_Pos7) ,EQU(Cfg_NumPos,8) NEQ(Wrk_Cmd,8) [XIC(Wrk_MaintTrig) ,XIC(Cfg_ViaPos1) ,NEQ(Wrk_Fdbk,8) ] OTE(Rdy_Pos8) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="84" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ALARM PROCESSING
============================================================
Pass the Cfg_PCmdClear configuration down to each P_Alarm instance.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear)OTE(PosFail.Cfg_PCmdClear)OTE(LockFail.Cfg_PCmdClear)OTE(IntlkTrip.Cfg_PCmdClear)OTE(IOFault.Cfg_PCmdClear);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="85" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The various alarms are ALWAYS allowed to Exist (Cfg_HasXxxAlarm can be 1), EXCEPT:
* If the device DOES NOT HAVE POSITION FEEDBACK, the Position Fail alarm will
never occur and should not exist.
* If the device DOES NOT HAVE THE LOCK FUNCTION OR LOCK FEEDBACK, the Lock
Fail alarm will never occur and should not exist.
(If the functions / feedbacks exist, the Fail alarms must be allowed to exist.)

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added PCfg_AllowExist on P_Alarm 3.0.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTL(IntlkTrip.PCfg_AllowExist) OTL(IOFault.PCfg_AllowExist) ,XIC(Cfg_HasPosFdbk) OTE(PosFail.PCfg_AllowExist) ,XIC(Cfg_HasLock) XIC(Cfg_HasLockFdbk) OTE(LockFail.PCfg_AllowExist) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="86" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Handle Failed to Reach Target Position Alarm Processing using the standard P_Alarm AOI.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[P_Alarm(PosFail);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="87" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Handle Failed to Lock / Unlock Alarm Processing using the standard P_Alarm AOI.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[P_Alarm(LockFail);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="88" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Handle Interlock Trip Alarm Processing using the standard P_Alarm AOI.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[P_Alarm(IntlkTrip);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="89" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Handle I/O Fault Alarm Processing using the standard P_Alarm AOI.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[P_Alarm(IOFault);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="90" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If ANY alarm is Disabled, Inhibited or Suppressed, set the Alarm Inhibit
summary status bit (which puts the "I" box on the graphic symbol).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(PosFail.Sts_AlmInh) ,XIC(LockFail.Sts_AlmInh) ,XIC(IntlkTrip.Sts_AlmInh) ,XIC(IOFault.Sts_AlmInh) ]OTE(Sts_AlmInh);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="91" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
NOTIFICATION VALUE
============================================================
Indicate the current alarm notification level as the max of any of the alarms,
and set the low-order bit for reset or ack required:
0 = Not in alarm, acknowledged
1 = Not in alarm, unacknowledged or reset required
2 = Low severity alarm, acknowledged
3 = Low severity alarm, unacknowledged
4 = Medium severity alarm, acknowledged
5 = Medium severity alarm, unacknowledged
6 = High severity alarm, acknowledged
7 = High severity alarm, unacknowledged
8 = Urgent severity alarm, acknowledged
9 = Urgent severity alarm, unacknowledged

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Separated Reset Reqd functions from Val_Notify  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_Notify) ,GRT(PosFail.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) MOV(PosFail.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) ,GRT(LockFail.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) MOV(LockFail.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) ,GRT(IntlkTrip.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) MOV(IntlkTrip.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) ,GRT(IOFault.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) MOV(IOFault.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) ,[XIC(PosFail.Val_Notify.0) ,XIC(LockFail.Val_Notify.0) ,XIC(IntlkTrip.Val_Notify.0) ,XIC(IOFault.Val_Notify.0) ] OTE(Wrk_Notify.0) ,MOV(Wrk_Notify,Val_Notify) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="92" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung identifies:
* if a latched Shed condition requires a reset in order to run the motor;
* if that reset or any alarm reset or other reset is required; and
* if any reset or acknowledge from the operator is required.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx), split from Val_Notify logic (above).  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[[XIC(PosFail.Rdy_Ack) ,XIC(LockFail.Rdy_Ack) ,XIC(IntlkTrip.Rdy_Ack) ,XIC(IOFault.Rdy_Ack) ] ,[XIC(PosFail.Rdy_Reset) ,XIC(LockFail.Rdy_Reset) ,XIC(IntlkTrip.Rdy_Reset) ,XIC(IOFault.Rdy_Reset) ,XIC(Nrdy_Fail) ,XIC(Nrdy_IOFault) XIO(Sts_IOFault) ] OTE(Rdy_Reset) ]OTE(Rdy_ResetAckAll);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Prescan" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Clear Ownership, set actual state to "moving", clear "lurking" Commands]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
PRESCAN (POWERUP) HANDLING
============================================================
On Prescan, set the Ownership to NO OWNER (0).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(PSet_Owner)CLR(Val_Owner);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA["Lurking" Program Commands are cleared if they are set as "Edge" triggered
(cleared by this object as received).
(Lurking Acknowledge Commands are left to perform their action.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear)[OTU(PCmd_Pos1) OTU(PCmd_Pos2) OTU(PCmd_Pos3) OTU(PCmd_Pos4) ,OTU(PCmd_Pos5) OTU(PCmd_Pos6) OTU(PCmd_Pos7) OTU(PCmd_Pos8) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA["Lurking" Operator Commands are cleared, as well as Program Reset.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(OCmd_Pos1) OTU(OCmd_Pos2) OTU(OCmd_Pos3) OTU(OCmd_Pos4) ,OTU(OCmd_Pos5) OTU(OCmd_Pos6) OTU(OCmd_Pos7) OTU(OCmd_Pos8) ,OTU(OCmd_Bypass) OTU(OCmd_Check) OTU(MCmd_Disable) OTU(MCmd_Enable) ,OTU(OCmd_Reset) OTU(OCmd_ResetAckAll) OTU(PCmd_Reset) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Override Command is set to NONE.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[On Prescan, clear device outputs.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_Out) OTU(Out_Pos1) OTU(Out_Pos2) OTU(Out_Pos3) OTU(Out_Pos4) ,OTU(Out_Pos5) OTU(Out_Pos6) OTU(Out_Pos7) OTU(Out_Pos8) ,OTU(Out_Inc) OTU(Out_Dec) OTU(Out_Unlock) OTU(Out_Lock) ,OTU(Out_CylExtend) OTU(Out_CylRetract) OTU(Out_CylLeft) OTU(Out_CylRight) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[On Prescan, clear the following:
Wrk_Cmd (no command active)
Wrk_Fdbk (device position not determined)
Wrk_State (state is powerup/unknown)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(Wrk_Cmd)CLR(Wrk_Fdbk)CLR(Wrk_State);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Clear the latched Shed faults and alarms, and reset the instruction's retry counter.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx).  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(Wrk_PosFail) OTU(Wrk_PosFailSts) OTU(Sts_PosFail) ,OTU(Wrk_LockFail) OTU(Wrk_LockFailSts) OTU(Sts_LockFail) OTU(Nrdy_IOFault) ,CLR(Wrk_RetryC) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[On Prescan, clear the following:
Val_Cmd (no command active)
Val_Fdbk (device position not determined)
Val_Sts (device not confirmed in position)
Val_State (state is powerup/unknown)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(Val_Cmd)CLR(Val_Fdbk)CLR(Val_Sts)CLR(Val_State);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
<Dependencies>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_40"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_20"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_16"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_12"/>
<Dependency Type="AddOnInstructionDefinition" Name="P_Alarm"/>
<Dependency Type="AddOnInstructionDefinition" Name="P_Mode"/>
</Dependencies>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
</AddOnInstructionDefinitions>
</Controller>
</RSLogix5000Content>
